 a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the original distribution is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {z}_{\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(Z>{z}_{\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2}$ and $Z∼N(0,1).$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $95%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.95=0.05\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.025.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(Z>1.96)=0.025.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{z}_{\\alpha /2}={z}_{0.025}=1.96.\n$$\n\nTherefore, a $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -5\\pm 1.96\\cdot \\frac{4.3}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & -5\\pm 1.69\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8b4c8931-ac30-564c-ba77-710890c7c3aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b4c8931-ac30-564c-ba77-710890c7c3aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b4c8931-ac30-564c-ba77-710890c7c3aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f81d09c4-1c72-5085-8688-6e7634892bfe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-16aed665-da6f-5199-b4a0-a23c3f6d73e6" "answer-cb0597e7-4186-5021-b1a9-df1e48a1d95c" "answer-f81d09c4-1c72-5085-8688-6e7634892bfe" "answer-63adfc45-4a04-5e67-9643-aa70578c5133" "answer-279474e9-ef4e-5abc-8ab4-8d1f3bd11164"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16aed665-da6f-5199-b4a0-a23c3f6d73e6" :answer/id #uuid "16aed665-da6f-5199-b4a0-a23c3f6d73e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\pm 1.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb0597e7-4186-5021-b1a9-df1e48a1d95c" :answer/id #uuid "cb0597e7-4186-5021-b1a9-df1e48a1d95c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\pm 1.45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f81d09c4-1c72-5085-8688-6e7634892bfe" :answer/id #uuid "f81d09c4-1c72-5085-8688-6e7634892bfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\pm 1.69" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63adfc45-4a04-5e67-9643-aa70578c5133" :answer/id #uuid "63adfc45-4a04-5e67-9643-aa70578c5133" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\pm 1.45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-279474e9-ef4e-5abc-8ab4-8d1f3bd11164" :answer/id #uuid "279474e9-ef4e-5abc-8ab4-8d1f3bd11164" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.3\\pm 1.69" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1c22a90f-9b7c-5ddf-a251-f5b0ff5c7b6d" :question/id #uuid "1c22a90f-9b7c-5ddf-a251-f5b0ff5c7b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142974" :question/problem "![](images/39/39a83b1081d22919c9549c4ff1c6ad8006dc802cc23f9802d762e97883bea48c.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n=32$ from a normal population with standard deviation $\\sigma =18.$ Given that the mean of the sample is $\\overset{―}{x}=-67,$ find a $90%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z>1.645)=0.05,$ where $Z∼N(0,1),$ as shown in the diagram above.*" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the population is normally distributed. Therefore, the distribution of sample mean is also normal, and we have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{\\sigma /\\sqrt{n}}∼N(0,1),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${\\sigma }^{2}$ is the population variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the original distribution is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {z}_{\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(Z>{z}_{\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2}$ and $Z∼N(0,1).$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $90%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.9=0.1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.05.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(Z>1.645)=0.05.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{z}_{\\alpha /2}={z}_{0.05}=1.645.\n$$\n\nTherefore, a $90%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-67\\pm 1.645\\cdot \\frac{18}{\\sqrt{32}} \\\\ -67\\pm 5.234\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-54346f0e-b0c5-52e5-ab1c-ea523499e32b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-54346f0e-b0c5-52e5-ab1c-ea523499e32b" :answer-field/id #uuid "54346f0e-b0c5-52e5-ab1c-ea523499e32b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8b9147f7-8d93-5f88-b745-147c1384f6d5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78403101-f6c5-5d61-aa5a-e0699c13fe11" "answer-8b9147f7-8d93-5f88-b745-147c1384f6d5" "answer-23f3c558-8e9a-5a12-bf1d-0fa1df352593" "answer-5a453aaf-5a79-5cd6-ac86-7dac361340d9" "answer-510dac73-7b74-5411-b745-977232bca39f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78403101-f6c5-5d61-aa5a-e0699c13fe11" :answer/id #uuid "78403101-f6c5-5d61-aa5a-e0699c13fe11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-67\\pm 12.407" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b9147f7-8d93-5f88-b745-147c1384f6d5" :answer/id #uuid "8b9147f7-8d93-5f88-b745-147c1384f6d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-67\\pm 5.234" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23f3c558-8e9a-5a12-bf1d-0fa1df352593" :answer/id #uuid "23f3c558-8e9a-5a12-bf1d-0fa1df352593" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-67\\pm 9.246" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a453aaf-5a79-5cd6-ac86-7dac361340d9" :answer/id #uuid "5a453aaf-5a79-5cd6-ac86-7dac361340d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\pm 10.468" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-510dac73-7b74-5411-b745-977232bca39f" :answer/id #uuid "510dac73-7b74-5411-b745-977232bca39f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\pm 6.028" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8fa7b8f1-fff9-5728-a4e4-0be7942c5cc6" :question/id #uuid "8fa7b8f1-fff9-5728-a4e4-0be7942c5cc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-142985" :question/problem "![](images/64/6486d3914bb0f7b4898220512e96630d13d2b0f4a5c1851938f98371a4c0255f.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n=49$ from a normal population with standard deviation $\\sigma =1.$ Given that the mean of the sample is $\\overset{―}{x}=12,$ find a $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z>2.576)=0.005,$ where $Z∼N(0,1),$ as shown in the diagram above.*" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the population is normally distributed. Therefore, the distribution of sample mean is also normal, and we have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{\\sigma /\\sqrt{n}}∼N(0,1),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${\\sigma }^{2}$ is the population variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the original distribution is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {z}_{\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(Z>{z}_{\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2}$ and $Z∼N(0,1).$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $99%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.99=0.01\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.005.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(Z>2.576)=0.005.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{z}_{\\alpha /2}={z}_{0.005}=2.576.\n$$\n\nTherefore, a $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & 12\\pm 2.576\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & 12\\pm 0.368\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0d089f46-9f14-525d-b921-4ddb01886d29"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0d089f46-9f14-525d-b921-4ddb01886d29" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d089f46-9f14-525d-b9