ue "properties of invertible matrices" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-86e5a0f2-8f10-5531-ae7d-52d463866902" :answer-field/id #uuid "86e5a0f2-8f10-5531-ae7d-52d463866902" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-726a5dc3-65f5-538d-af5b-3ba8daedca86" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e0da1ffb-345f-5ae1-91cb-7693db413e1a" "answer-4ef6c5e9-0b48-5bca-8fc3-2d7acdfe98a9" "answer-726a5dc3-65f5-538d-af5b-3ba8daedca86" "answer-83149379-a893-5cb3-ad7b-b43718777042"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0da1ffb-345f-5ae1-91cb-7693db413e1a" :answer/id #uuid "e0da1ffb-345f-5ae1-91cb-7693db413e1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ef6c5e9-0b48-5bca-8fc3-2d7acdfe98a9" :answer/id #uuid "4ef6c5e9-0b48-5bca-8fc3-2d7acdfe98a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-726a5dc3-65f5-538d-af5b-3ba8daedca86" :answer/id #uuid "726a5dc3-65f5-538d-af5b-3ba8daedca86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83149379-a893-5cb3-ad7b-b43718777042" :answer/id #uuid "83149379-a893-5cb3-ad7b-b43718777042" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311314 :answer-field/correct 17592186310617 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186310913 :answer-field/correct 17592186308916 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-d656b9e3-27c9-51a6-a70f-c9d56643be83" :question/id #uuid "d656b9e3-27c9-51a6-a70f-c9d56643be83" :question/math-academy-id "q-336108" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-3}} by the transitive property of equality." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Once ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis, every solution $x(t)$ of the system can be expressed uniquely as a linear combination\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{the definition of a basis}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are the columns of $Φ(t),$ we can write\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen by the definition of matrix multiplication,\n\n$$\nΦ(t)\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of matrix multiplication}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ In $\\text{L3}$ we have $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t),$ and in $\\text{L4}$ we have $Φ(t)c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).$ Since both expressions are equal to the same quantity, the transitive property of equality gives $x(t)=Φ(t)c.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L3 and L4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-84273087-2e18-501d-872d-5ad466c8d262" "answer-field-69513af4-694f-5ca8-996c-0c33d8fa859d" "answer-field-3b347ff5-a360-5553-944a-1fd66d4ece0a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-84273087-2e18-501d-872d-5ad466c8d262" :answer-field/id #uuid "84273087-2e18-501d-872d-5ad466c8d262" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-f03bcfca-1c79-5dcc-a769-287b903a87de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0c1b43a8-0bad-584d-8658-946b10a53deb" "answer-fd8a0c7f-af95-54f9-89f1-fb7222915fbd" "answer-fd2fe107-c83d-541c-ad1f-d9f4feb898de" "answer-f03bcfca-1c79-5dcc-a769-287b903a87de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c1b43a8-0bad-584d-8658-946b10a53deb" :answer/id #uuid "0c1b43a8-0bad-584d-8658-946b10a53deb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd8a0c7f-af95-54f9-89f1-fb7222915fbd" :answer/id #uuid "fd8a0c7f-af95-54f9-89f1-fb7222915fbd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd2fe107-c83d-541c-ad1f-d9f4feb898de" :answer/id #uuid "fd2fe107-c83d-541c-ad1f-d9f4feb898de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplying $Φ(t)$ with its inverse" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f03bcfca-1c79-5dcc-a769-287b903a87de" :answer/id #uuid "f03bcfca-1c79-5dcc-a769-287b903a87de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69513af4-694f-5ca8-996c-0c33d8fa859d" :answer-field/id #uuid "69513af4-694f-5ca8-996c-0c33d8fa859d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ce4515ff-f000-5d07-9351-f9cf05460b2d" :answer-field/choices ["answer